# The released agents binary, which the devtools phase hands to
# git/install-hooks.sh as the path the four hook names point at. A qualified name
# taps on demand, so this list needs no separate `tap` line -- and nothing builds
# agents from the checkout any more.
#
# The packaging phase trusts this tap before `brew bundle` runs
# (trustBrewfileTaps, internal/phase/packages.go): Homebrew refuses to LOAD a
# formula from an untrusted third-party tap, which is what stopped the tap
# installing on both Linux CI images. The tap is read off this file, so the
# trusted set and the installed set cannot drift.
brew "nilbot/tap/agents"

